 and Sprint","classification":"same_identity","rationale":"It contains the same planned sprint approach, braking, planted half-turn, and opposite-direction reacceleration; the source card has been archived and retained as an alias.","distinguishingDimensions":{"identityDifference":"none","deliveryDifferences":["approach_distance","turn_style","terminal_stick_option"]}},{"name":"Modified 505","classification":"new_variant","rationale":"A standardized 5-meter approach, 180-degree turn, and 5-meter exit preserve the identity while fixing testing distances, line rules, timing, and trial validity.","distinguishingDimensions":{"approach":"5_meters","exit":"5_meters","context":"standardized_assessment"}},{"name":"Traditional 505","classification":"new_variant","rationale":"A flying approach raises entry velocity and testing demand but retains one planned 180-degree turn and reacceleration.","distinguishingDimensions":{"approach":"flying_longer_approach","entryVelocity":"higher","context":"standardized_assessment"}},{"name":"Reactive 180-Degree Turn on Cue","classification":"new_definition","rationale":"An unpredictable cue adds perception, decision, and response-time demands and is reactive agility rather than planned COD.","distinguishingDimensions":{"cue":"unpredictable","decisionDemand":"direction_choice"}},{"name":"5-10-5 Pro Agility Shuttle","classification":"new_definition","rationale":"The two-turn, three-segment shuttle has a different route, contact sequence, side order, fatigue profile, and timing outcome.","distinguishingDimensions":{"turnCount":2,"route":"5_10_5","contactSequence":"two_opposed_turns"}}]}$card_1_payload$::JSONB);
